sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant NextJS as Next.js App
    participant BetterAuth as Better-Auth
    participant Databricks as Databricks Workspace
    participant Postgres as Postgres Database

    User->>NextJS: Click "Login with Workspace"
    NextJS->>User: Show Workspace Selector
    User->>NextJS: Enter workspace URL

    NextJS->>BetterAuth: Initiate workspace OAuth<br/>(workspace_url provided)

    Note over BetterAuth: Generate state & PKCE params<br/>Store workspace_url in state

    BetterAuth->>User: Redirect to Workspace OAuth
    Note over User,Databricks: URL: {workspace_url}/oidc/v1/authorize

    User->>Databricks: Workspace Login Page
    User->>Databricks: Authenticate
    Databricks->>Databricks: Verify user permissions<br/>in workspace

    Databricks->>User: Redirect with auth code
    User->>NextJS: Callback with code

    NextJS->>BetterAuth: Handle callback
    BetterAuth->>BetterAuth: Verify state
    BetterAuth->>BetterAuth: Extract workspace_url

    BetterAuth->>Databricks: Exchange code for tokens<br/>at {workspace_url}/oidc/v1/token
    Databricks->>BetterAuth: access_token, refresh_token,<br/>id_token, expires_in

    BetterAuth->>BetterAuth: Decode id_token JWT
    Note over BetterAuth: Extract claims:<br/>- sub (user ID)<br/>- email<br/>- name<br/>- workspace_id

    BetterAuth->>Postgres: Upsert User record
    Postgres-->>BetterAuth: User ID

    BetterAuth->>Postgres: Query or create Organization<br/>(mapped to workspace)
    Note over Postgres: Organization can map to<br/>multiple workspaces
    Postgres-->>BetterAuth: Organization ID

    BetterAuth->>Postgres: Create Workspace record<br/>if not exists
    Note over Postgres: Store workspace_id,<br/>workspace_url, org mapping

    BetterAuth->>Postgres: Create/Update Account<br/>(provider: databricks-workspace)
    Note over Postgres: Account linked to:<br/>- User<br/>- Workspace<br/>- Organization
    Postgres-->>BetterAuth: Account ID

    BetterAuth->>Postgres: Store encrypted tokens<br/>in OAuth_Token
    Note over Postgres: Separate tokens per workspace<br/>Each token scoped to workspace

    BetterAuth->>Postgres: Add user to OrganizationMember<br/>if not exists
    Note over Postgres: Default role: member<br/>Can be promoted by admin

    BetterAuth->>Postgres: Create Session<br/>with activeOrganizationId
    Note over Postgres: Session context:<br/>- Current user<br/>- Active organization<br/>- Available workspaces

    Postgres-->>BetterAuth: Session created

    BetterAuth->>NextJS: Set session cookie
    NextJS->>User: Redirect to dashboard

    User->>NextJS: Make API call to workspace
    NextJS->>BetterAuth: Get session
    BetterAuth->>Postgres: Query session + active org
    Postgres-->>BetterAuth: Session with org context

    BetterAuth->>Postgres: Get workspace OAuth token<br/>for active org
    Note over Postgres: Retrieve correct token<br/>for target workspace
    Postgres-->>BetterAuth: Decrypted access_token

    BetterAuth->>NextJS: Return token for API call
    NextJS->>Databricks: API call with token
    Databricks-->>NextJS: API response
    NextJS->>User: Show data
